# 0876. Middle of the Linked List

**Language:** Java

## Difficulty

Easy

## Topics

- Linked List
- Two Pointers

## Problem Statement

Given the head of a singly linked list, return the middle node of the linked list.

If there are two middle nodes, return the second middle node.

## Approach

This solution uses the **slow and fast pointer technique**.

- Initialize two pointers, `slow` and `fast`, at the head of the list.
- Move `slow` one node at a time.
- Move `fast` two nodes at a time.
- Continue until `fast` reaches the end of the list or `fast.next` becomes `null`.
- When the loop ends, `slow` will be pointing to the middle node.
- If the list has an even number of nodes, `slow` naturally points to the second middle node, as required.

## Complexity Analysis

- **Time Complexity:** O(n)
- **Space Complexity:** O(1)

## Java Solution

See `Solution.java` for the complete implementation.